          "user_content": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "Invoice totals come out short.\n\n`invoice_total(amounts)` in `src/invoices/report.py` adds up the line amounts, but a $19.99 line and a $5.50 line total $24.00 instead of $25.49 -- the cents are being lost. Please fix the root cause so totals are exact."
              }
            ],
            "role": "user"
          },
          "final_response": {
            "parts": [
              {
                "text": "The root cause of the issue was in `src/invoices/load.py`, where the `parse_amount` function was casting the parsed float to an `int`, effectively truncating the decimal portion of the invoice amounts.\n\nI have updated `src/invoices/load.py` to return the `float` value directly, preserving the cents.\n\n```python\n# src/invoices/load.py\n\ndef parse_amount(raw):\n    \"\"\"Parse a raw dollar amount into a number.\"\"\"\n    return float(raw)\n```\n\nThis change ensures that `invoice_total` in `src/invoices/report.py` receives the correct floating-point values, allowing it to calculate the total accurately.",
